# K01 witness (steps/k01-selector-identity-20261001.md §6): occurrence selectors through an
# admitted formal.  Pair carries two x, Triple three.  A value admitted by name must give
# ITS last x for bare `v\x` and ITS second occurrence for `v\[1]x`; both uses resolve to
# the requirement's field 1, which is why one slot map per requirement field cannot serve
# them.  `off(p)` = 20 - 20 = 0 (Pair's own layout); `off(t)` = 30 - 20 = 10.  Success is 7.
Pair: (size_t: x 10U; size_t: x 20U)
Triple: (size_t: x 10U; size_t: x 20U; size_t: x 30U)
fn: off (Pair: v) int
    size_t: last
    size_t: second
    last: v\x
    second: v\[1]x
    return: (cast: (int) (last - second))
end: off
Pair: p
Triple: t
int: ok 7
if: off(p) != 0
    ok: 81
if: off(t) != 10
    ok: 82
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
